{
  "name": "beluga",
  "_about": "THE BELUGA (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/bigmam/beluga.py, built from scratch on the dolphin's plan): a white whale, 4 m -- the big round BULBOUS MELON over a short stubby beak (a short mouth turned up at the corner), a real NECK (a narrowing and a fold behind the head; the rig's own neck bone turns the head side to side), NO dorsal fin but a low rough DORSAL RIDGE along the rear half of the back, a stout body, short broad rounded PADDLE flippers, broad flukes with a convex wavy trailing edge. Coats: white (adult), creamy (the summer's yellowed skin), grey (a young one, smaller). A swimmer (`fly`); its tail pitches. Written whole by its script.",
